<#ftl output_format="HTML" auto_esc=true>
<#-- features comes from sample FeaturesAdvice calling native evaluateAll on the request context. -->
<#macro badge value><span class="badge ${value?then('on','off')}">${value?then('ON','OFF')}</span></#macro>
<#macro presets><div class="presets"><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="matching">Matching preset</button></form><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="nonmatching">Non-matching preset</button></form></div></#macro>
<#macro table keys><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Flag key</th><th>Definition</th><th>This request</th></tr></thead><tbody><#list keys as key><tr data-flag="${key}"><td><code>${key}</code></td><td>${definitions?seq_contains(key)?then('Present','Absent')}</td><td><@badge value=(features[key])!false/><#if key == 'filter-device-type'> <small>Macintosh detection unsupported in core 1.6.0</small></#if></td></tr></#list></tbody></table></div></#macro>
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>${title} · Java Spring Boot SDK Sample</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><script src="/workshop.js" defer></script></head><body>
<header><p class="eyebrow">TOGGLY / JAVA SPRING BOOT</p><a class="brand" href="/">Feature flag workshop</a><p>Learn the published Boot starter, one request at a time.</p></header>
<nav aria-label="Sections"><#list paths as link><a href="${link}">${titles[link?index]}</a></#list></nav><main>
<#if !configured><aside class="warning" role="status"><strong>Missing TOGGLY_APP_KEY — unconfigured offline mode.</strong> Starter auto-configuration is off. No live evaluations or synthetic enabled flags. Protected examples deny with 503. <a href="/configuration">Set up your app</a>.</aside>
<#else><aside class="status">Signed definitions configured · ${definitions?size} current definitions · HTTP poll every 60 seconds in normal startup. Reload to see current evaluations.</aside><#if definitions?size == 0><aside class="warning">No definitions available yet. Missing flags use false defaults; check your key, environment and connection.</aside></#if></#if>
<#if errors gt 0><aside class="warning">SDK refresh errors observed: ${errors}. The SDK retains its last valid signed definitions. This cumulative warning remains after recovery; inspect current flags and retry refresh.</aside></#if>
<p class="context">User: <strong>${identity?has_content?then(identity,'anonymous')}</strong> · Order: <strong>${order}</strong> · Demo identities are not authentication.</p><h1>${title}</h1>
<#switch path>
<#case '/'>
<p>Follow the sections from a Boolean flag to isolated users, Orders and Boot-native annotations.</p><div class="cards"><#list paths as link><#if link != '/' ><a class="card" href="${link}"><span>${link?index}</span><h2>${titles[link?index]}</h2></a></#if></#list></div>
<h2>First flag exercise</h2><ol><li>Complete Configuration and create <code>new-dashboard</code> in Production.</li><li>Enable it, wait up to 60 seconds or use Refresh in Spring Boot integration.</li><li>Open Declarative gates: the feature route allows and the negate route denies.</li><li>Disable the flag, refresh, and observe the opposite HTTP result. The <code>@ConditionalOnFeature</code> startup copy does not change until you restart.</li></ol>
<h2>Flag checklist and current snapshot</h2><p>When configured, sample model advice calls native <code>evaluateAll</code> for this request before the template renders. Absent means the key is missing from current definitions, not simply OFF.</p><@table keys=flags/><p><a href="/api/evaluate">Programmatic JSON snapshot</a></p>
<#break>
<#case '/gates'>
<p>Native <code>@FeatureEnabled</code> is AOP on <code>FeatureService</code>. The controller translates the Boolean into HTTP 200/404. The starter has no <code>@FeatureGate</code> and no negate attribute — the negate route inverts the dashboard Boolean in sample code.</p>
<div class="cards"><article class="card"><h2>Feature</h2><@badge value=(features['new-dashboard'])!false/><p><a href="/gated/feature">Try feature route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>Negate</h2><@badge value=configured && !((features['new-dashboard'])!false)/><p><a href="/gated/negate">Try negate route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ALL: dashboard + API v2</h2><@badge value=allOn/><p><a href="/gated/all">Try ALL route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ANY: dashboard + API v2</h2><@badge value=anyOn/><p><a href="/gated/any">Try ANY route</a></p></article></div>
<h2>Per-request template vs startup bean</h2>
<#if (features['new-dashboard'])!false><p id="dashboard-content">New dashboard content is visible.</p><#else><p id="dashboard-content">Classic dashboard fallback is visible.</p></#if>
<p>The sentence above follows this request. Startup bean copy: <strong>${startupCopy}</strong> — selected once by <code>@ConditionalOnFeature</code>.</p>
<h2>Variants</h2><aside class="note">Native variant allocation is unsupported in io.toggly core/starter 1.6.0. No variant is fabricated. <code>getValue</code> selects between two caller-provided values using a Boolean flag; telemetry variant labels do not allocate experiments.</aside>
<#break>
<#case '/programmatic'>
<p>Use explicit immutable context for service code. Native <code>getValue</code> selects a Boolean branch, not a variant. <code>@FeatureEnabled</code> is the starter's method gate; HTTP status is sample composition.</p><pre>client.isEnabled("api-v2", context)
client.gate(List.of("new-dashboard", "api-v2"),
    FeatureRequirement.ALL, false, context)
client.evaluateAll(context)
client.getValue("api-v2", "v2", "v1")
@FeatureEnabled("enhanced-submit")</pre>
<p>Current API version: <strong>${apiVersion}</strong></p><p><a href="/api/evaluate">Open current request JSON</a> · <a href="/api/flag/unknown">Unknown flag defaults false</a></p><form method="post" action="/actions/submit"><button>Try enhanced submit</button></form><p>Submit calls <code>@FeatureEnabled("enhanced-submit")</code> then returns 403 when disabled. No order is persisted. Unconfigured actions return 503.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/identity'>
<p>A session stores demo inputs, never evaluated flag results. <code>DemoContextFilter</code> constructs immutable identity, claims, request fields and Order and clears ContextHolder after every request, including errors.</p><@presets/>
<h2>Customize this session</h2><form class="fields" method="post" action="/context"><label>Identity<input name="identity" maxlength="512" value="${identity}"></label><label>Claim role<input name="role" maxlength="512" value="${role}"></label><label>Country<input name="country" maxlength="512" value="${country}"></label><label>Accept-Language<input name="language" maxlength="512" value="${language}"></label><label>User-Agent<input name="userAgent" maxlength="512" value="${userAgent}"></label><label>Order<select name="order"><option value="vip"<#if order == 'ord-vip'> selected</#if>>ord-vip</option><option value="standard"<#if order != 'ord-vip'> selected</#if>>ord-standard</option></select></label><button>Apply session context</button></form><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="clear">Clear session identity</button></form>
<p>Initial anonymous requests read actual User-Agent, Accept-Language and cf-ipcountry headers where present. Presets deliberately override these fields. These local controls are not trusted authentication.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/orders'>
<p>User identity stays the same while the entity changes. These checks run side by side in one request using <code>context.withEntity(...)</code>, with kind Order, Id, Vip and Total.</p><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h2>ord-vip · Vip=true</h2><span id="vip-result"><@badge value=vipOn/></span><p><a href="/orders?order=vip">Select VIP for this request</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ord-standard · Vip=false</h2><span id="standard-result"><@badge value=standardOn/></span><p><a href="/orders?order=standard">Select standard for this request</a></p></article></div><p>Without an entity: <span id="missing-result"><@badge value=missingOn/></span> · <a href="/orders?order=missing">Try missing entity</a></p><pre>var order = new TogglyEntityContext("Order", "ord-vip",
    Map.of("Id", "ord-vip", "Vip", true, "Total", 250));
client.isEnabled("ExpressCheckout", context.withEntity(order));</pre><p>Never reuse a Boolean result across different Orders. The published engine compares attributes without enforcing definition.contextKind; this app explicitly constructs Order at its boundary. A missing entity evaluates false.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/filters'>
<p>All eleven rows use native evaluation. Apply a saved preset or compare one request without changing your session.</p><@presets/><p><a href="/filters?preset=matching">Matching for this request</a> · <a href="/filters?preset=nonmatching">Non-matching for this request</a></p><@table keys=filters/>
<p>AlwaysOn stays ON for both; TimeWindow stays ON during 2020–2099. Percentage is sticky per identity and flag, so Alice/Bob are not prescribed ON/OFF. The seven other supported segment/context rows should be ON for Matching and OFF for Non-matching. DeviceType Macintosh is a native SDK gap: the parser recognizes iPhone/iPad/iPod but returns Other for desktop Macintosh. The exact shared rule remains OFF.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/boot'>
<h2>Native Boot pipeline</h2><ol><li>With a key, <code>toggly.enabled=true</code> activates starter <code>TogglyAutoConfiguration</code>.</li><li>This sample supplies <code>TogglyConfig</code> (signed, no WebSocket) and a Spring-owned <code>HttpSnapshotProvider</code>. The starter's null provider bean is not injectable on Boot 3.5.16.</li><li>Starter constructs <code>TogglyClient</code>. <code>FeatureAspect</code> is registered here; it is not an auto-config bean.</li><li><code>DemoContextFilter</code> installs request-scoped ContextHolder before AOP or controllers run, then clears it.</li><li><code>@FeatureEnabled</code> and <code>@ConditionalOnFeature</code> are the starter's annotations. HTTP 404/403 is sample translation.</li><li>Actuator exposes <code>/actuator/health</code> (toggly indicator) and <code>/actuator/toggly</code> using process default context, not this request.</li></ol>
<p><a href="/gated/beta">Try beta-access AOP gate</a> · <a href="/native/argument">Try FeatureEnabled targeting</a></p>
<p>This host is Spring Boot <strong>3.5.16</strong>, the version declared by published starter 1.6.0. Boot 4.1.1 fails native Actuator startup because <code>TogglyHealthIndicator</code> still implements the Boot 3 <code>org.springframework.boot.actuate.health.HealthIndicator</code> type.</p>
<p><a href="/actuator/health">Open /actuator/health</a> · <a href="/actuator/toggly">Open /actuator/toggly</a></p>
<form data-native-refresh method="post" action="/api/refresh"><button>Request native definitions refresh</button></form><output id="refresh-result" aria-live="polite"></output>
<h2>Thread lifetime</h2><p>ContextHolder is thread-local. This app uses synchronous MVC and eight Tomcat workers. Pass immutable EvaluationContext into executors; do not assume the holder flows off-thread.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/configuration'>
<h2>Connect your own application</h2><ol><li>Open app.toggly.io and use a workspace you can manage (the one from signup is enough).</li><li>Create <strong>Java Spring Boot SDK Sample</strong>; select <strong>Java</strong> technology and <strong>Production</strong> environment.</li><li>Set Application URL to <code>http://localhost:8090</code>. Add allowed origins only if that client-side section is present.</li><li>Add Order with Id string key, Vip boolean and Total optional number.</li><li>Create all sixteen flags and the Filters category using the README recipe.</li><li>Copy .env.example to .env, set your key locally, export it, and restart.</li></ol><p>Never commit a real key. The missing-key app makes no Toggly requests and has no synthetic live data.</p><h2>Loading, refresh and errors</h2><p>Startup attempts signed definitions. Unknown flags default false. The native provider can fetch again on empty snapshots, polls every 60 seconds and retains last valid definitions after network or signature failures. Pages reevaluate the current context; results are never stored in sessions.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/allowed'><p>The published FeatureAspect allowed the service method; the controller then rendered this page.</p><@table keys=flags/><#break>
</#switch>
</main><footer>Published io.toggly starter 1.6.0 · Spring Boot 3.5.16 · Java 17 · Actuator health + /actuator/toggly</footer></body></html>
